    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Putnam County",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8256\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town of Southeast, county of\nPutnam, to alienate certain lands used as parkland and to dedicate\ncertain other lands as parklands\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAuthorizing the town of Southeast, county of Putnam, to alienate certain\nlands used as parkland and to dedicate certain other lands as parklands\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: The town of Southeast, county of Putnam is authorized to\ndiscontinue parkland described in section 3 and alienate it and convey\nit to Proswing Sports Realty, INC. for the purpose of developing such\nlands from being used for any other purpose other than recreation as may\nbe defined by the town of Southeast zoning code.  1\n\nSection 2: This act shall be effective only when the Proswing Sports\nRealty, INC conveys to the town of Southeast described in section 4 and\nthe town of Southeast dedicated the lands as parklands, provided that\nthe town of Southeast has never used such lands for public open space or\npark purposes.\n\nSection 3: Metes and bounds description of the land to be alienated by\nthe town of Southeast, county of Putnam and conveyed to Proswing Sports\nRealty, INC.\n\nSection 4: Metes and bounds description of land to be conveyed to the\ntown of Southeast, county of Putnam.\n\nSection 5: In the event that the fair market value of the parklands\ndescribed in Section 4 that will be dedicated by the town of Southeast\nis not equal to or greater than the fair market value of the parklands\nbeing alienated as described in Section 3, the town of Southeast shall\ndedicate the difference towards the acquisition of new parklands and/or\ntowards capital improvements to existing park and recreational facili-\nties.\n\nSection 6: Provides that if the town of Southeast receives federal fund-\ning for the purchase, maintenance or improvement of the parklands, the\ndiscontinuance of parkland shall not occur until the town of Southeast\nhas complied with federal regulations.\n\nSection 7: States effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nNot applicable at this time.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town Board of the Town of Southeast has requested Home Rule Legis-\nlation to authorize the Town Board to alienate a portion of Town-owned\nparkland on Pugsley Road.The conveyance of the Pugsley Road site shall\nbe specifically conditioned upon such site being deed restricted to\nprohibit the site from being used for any purpose other than Recreation\nas may be defined by the Town of Southeast.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThere are no fiscal implications to the state or local governments asso-\nciated with the passage of this legislation.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
